      "observed": "The STM32L476 VBAT pin is explicitly left as a no-connect: netlist net 64 contains only U2 pin 1 VBAT with pintype \"power_in+no_connect\".",
      "expected": "For an STM32L476 without an external backup battery, the VBAT power input should normally be tied to the main VCC/VDD supply rather than left floating. The specification notes that no battery/regulator/USB source is shown, but it does not sanction leaving a power input pin unconnected.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"64\") (name \"unconnected-(U2-VBAT-Pad1)\") (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\") (pintype \"power_in+no_connect\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(pin (num \"1\") (name \"VBAT\") (type \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "the schematic does not show where board VCC is normally sourced from (no battery, regulator, or USB part appears anywhere in the three `.kicad_sch` files or `PCB.net`/`PCB.cir`"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The backup domain may be unpowered or floating, which can cause leakage, unreliable power-up behavior, and loss of RTC/backup-domain functions. The core MCU may still operate, but this is a deviation from standard STM32 power design practice.",
      "confidence": 0.65
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The main connectivity and passive values match the specification, but U2's VBAT power pin is left as an explicit no-connect, which is inconsistent with standard STM32L4 practice when no backup battery is used."
}

